  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Two tourists are walking 12 km apart along the same flat track in the same direction at a constant speed of 4 km/h. When each tourist reaches the slope of a mountain, they climb it along the same route at a constant speed of 3 km/h. What is the distance, in kilometres, separating the two tourists once both are climbing?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p21-q10-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "9\\text{ km}",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p21-q10-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "They reach the slope 3 hours apart, so their separation during the climb is 3 × 3 km.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The second tourist reaches the slope after the first by\n$$\\begin{align*}t&=\\frac{d}{s}\\\\t&=\\frac{12}{4}\\\\t&=3\\text{ h}.\\end{align*}$$\nIn those 3 hours, the first tourist climbs\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=st\\\\d&=3\\times3\\\\d&=9\\text{ km}.\\end{align*}$$\nOnce both tourists are climbing at the same speed, their separation remains 9 km.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 78
  },
